        "original_id": "a1ac8d4d-6c76-574c-9765-9803807de36b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Constantine, Chas Chandler, Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, John Totleben, Jamie Delano, Philip Bond\n- Companies: DC Comics, Vertigo\n- Products: Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood, Northlanders\n- Roles: antihero, sidekick, cab driver\n\nFacts:\n- John Constantine first appeared in The Saga of the Swamp Thing No. 25 in June 1984.\n- Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, and John Totleben created John Constantine.\n- John Constantine is a fictional antihero who appears in comic books published by DC Comics and its alternative imprint Vertigo.\n- Chas Chandler is John Constantine's closest and longest surviving friend, and Chas Chandler acts as his sidekick and cab driver.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood was written by Jamie Delano and illustrated by Philip Bond.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood features John Constantine several decades after most of his series continuity.\n- Northlanders is an American comic book series published by DC Comics under its Vertigo imprint.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
